ctually invoked from `check_time_to_probe_bw`, they won't need the annotation. I'm second-guessing whether `#[allow(dead_code)]` on an `impl` block actually propagates to the methods inside—I should just add the attribute to each of the 5 methods individually to be safe. Actually, the simplest approach might be to write a test that exercises the early return path in `check_startup_resume` and make those private helpers `pub(crate)` instead, which would eliminate the dead code warnings altogether.\n\nLooking at this more carefully from a testing angle: `check_time_to_cruise` needs a `Path` argument to call `inflight_with_headroom` and `inflight_with_bw`, but constructing a minimal `Path` is difficult since it's defined in internal.rs with many fields. Let me examine what `inflight_with_headroom` actually requires...\n\nExamining function signatures... I see the issue now—when `inflight_with_headroom` returns `u64::MAX`, the bytes-in-transit check passes through, but then we hit `inflight_with_bw` which requires the `send_mtu` field from `path_x`. Let me trace through what `inflight_with_bw` actually needs... I'm seeing that no matter which path I take through the code—whether `min_rtt` is at its max value or I set both `max_bw` and `min_rtt` to zero—the calculation always bottlenecks on needing `path_x.send_mtu`. The `Path` struct is carrying a lot of weight here, and it seems unavoidable.\n\nLet me check if `Path` has a `Default` implementation I could leverage to construct a minimal version.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":542,"cache_read_input_tokens":114557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":542},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f812e07-a4f7-4714-a4da-eb4436fecbda","uuid":"3095675a-a498-43a3-8b64-69dff70e88bb"}
